---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | CENIT e.V."
  canonical="https://cenit-ev.de/en/privacy/"
  description="Privacy policy of CENIT e.V. pursuant to Art. 13 GDPR – information on hosting, cookies, and your rights."
  robotsNoindex
>
  <main class="cenit-page">
    <section class="cenit-section cenit-section-narrow">
      <div class="cenit-container cenit-text">
        <header class="cenit-legal-header">
          <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p>Information pursuant to Art. 13 GDPR</p>
        </header>
        <section>
          <h2>1. General Information</h2>
          <p>
            The protection of your personal data is important to us.
            We process your data exclusively in accordance with the applicable legal provisions
            (GDPR, BDSG).
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>2. Controller</h2>
          <p>
            CENIT – Association for the Promotion of Interdisciplinary Dance Medicine e.V.<br>
            Knesebeckstr. 20<br>
            10623 Berlin<br>
            Germany<br><br>
            E-Mail: info@cenit-ev.de
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>3. Hosting</h2>
          <p>
            Our website is hosted by an external service provider:
          </p>
          <p>
            Vercel Inc.<br>
            440 N Barranca Ave #4133<br>
            Covina, CA 91723<br>
            USA
          </p>
          <p>
            When you visit our website, the hosting provider automatically collects and stores
            information in so-called server log files. This includes in particular:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>IP address</li>
            <li>Date and time of the request</li>
            <li>Browser type and version</li>
            <li>Operating system</li>
            <li>Referrer URL</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Processing is carried out on the basis of Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR
            (legitimate interest), as it is necessary for the secure and stable
            operation of the website.
          </p>
          <p>
            Data transfer to the USA is based on the European Commission’s
            standard contractual clauses.
          </p>
          <p>
            Further information:
            <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>4. Access Data (Server Log Files)</h2>
          <p>
            When visiting our website, general technical information is automatically collected.
            This includes:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>IP address</li>
            <li>Date and time of access</li>
            <li>Browser type and version</li>
            <li>Operating system</li>
            <li>Referrer URL</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            This data is technically necessary to correctly deliver the website
            and is not used to identify you personally.
          </p>
          <p>
            Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest).
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>5. Embedded Content (Infogram)</h2>
          <p>
            Our website includes interactive charts provided by Infogram (Infogram Inc.).
          </p>
          <p>
            These contents are only loaded after you actively consent via our cookie settings tool
            (see section 7) or click on "Show chart". Only then is a connection to Infogram
            servers established.
          </p>
          <p>
            In the process, the following data may be transmitted:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>IP address</li>
            <li>Browser and device information</li>
            <li>Referrer URL</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Processing is based on your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, § 25(1) TDDDG). You can withdraw
            your consent at any time via the "Cookie Settings" link in the footer of the website.
          </p>
          <p>
            Further information:
            <a href="https://infogram.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              https://infogram.com/privacy
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>6. Own Media Content (Video)</h2>
          <p>
            We provide our own video content, which is delivered directly via our servers.
          </p>
          <p>
            No personal data is transmitted to third parties in this context.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>7. Web Analytics (Google Analytics)</h2>
          <p>
            This website uses Google Analytics 4, a web analytics service provided by Google Ireland
            Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland ("Google").
          </p>
          <p>
            Google Analytics uses technologies that enable analysis of your usage behaviour (e.g.
            cookies or device fingerprinting). The information collected is generally transmitted to
            and stored on a Google server in the USA.
          </p>
          <p>
            We have enabled IP anonymisation. Your IP address is therefore shortened by Google within
            member states of the European Union or in other contracting states of the Agreement on the
            European Economic Area prior to transmission.
          </p>
          <p>
            Google Analytics is only loaded if you have previously given your active consent. We use our
            own lightweight consent banner for this purpose, which is shown to you on
            your first visit. Processing is based on your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, § 25(1) TDDDG).
            Without your consent, no Google Analytics script is loaded and no connection to Google
            servers is established.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can withdraw your consent at any time with future effect by clicking the "Cookie
            Settings" link in the footer of any page and adjusting your selection. Alternatively, you can
            generally prevent the collection of your data by Google Analytics by downloading and
            installing the browser plugin available at:
            <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout
            </a>
          </p>
          <p>
            Further information:
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              https://policies.google.com/privacy
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
          <p>You have the right to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
            <li>Objection (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>9. Right to Lodge a Complaint</h2>
          <p>
            You have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* CENIT-Stil für rechtliche Seiten (Impressum/Legal Notice/Privacy/Datenschutz) */
  .cenit-page {
    padding: 48px 0 64px;
  }
  .cenit-section-narrow .cenit-container {
    max-width: var(--cenit-axis-760);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .cenit-legal-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .cenit-legal-header h1 {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 32px;
    color: var(--cenit-purple);
    margin: 0 0 8px 0;
  }
  .cenit-legal-header p {
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cenit-container.cenit-text > section {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .cenit-container.cenit-text h2 {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--cenit-purple);
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  }
  .cenit-container.cenit-text p,
  .cenit-container.cenit-text ul {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--cenit-text);
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  }
  .cenit-container.cenit-text ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .cenit-container.cenit-text li {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .cenit-container.cenit-text a {
    color: var(--cenit-purple);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
